== an empty http_proxy reads HTTP_PROXY
http://g.test:<http>/ 200 http g.test:<http>/
proxy: g.test:<http>
== '' is empty; ALL_PROXY when the scheme's is unset
http://al.test:<http>/ 200 http al.test:<http>/
https://localhost:<https>/al 200 https localhost:<https>/al
proxy: al.test:<http>
proxy: localhost:<https>
== ALL_PROXY naming a SOCKS proxy is ignored
http://localhost:<http>/so 200 http localhost:<http>/so
== https:// and socks5:// proxies are ignored
http://localhost:<http>/x 200 http localhost:<http>/x
https://localhost:<https>/y 200 https localhost:<https>/y
== the variables read at each request
http://o1.test:<http>/a 200 http o1.test:<http>/a
env:http_proxy=
http://o2.test:<http>/b failed
env:http_proxy=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>
env:NO_PROXY=o3.test
http://o3.test:<http>/c failed
http://o4.test:<http>/d 200 http o4.test:<http>/d
proxy: o1.test:<http>
proxy: o4.test:<http>
== NO_PROXY
http://x.n1.test:<http>/ failed
http://n2.test:<http>/ failed
http://xn1.test:<http>/ 200 http xn1.test:<http>/
http://[::1]:<http>/ failed
http://127.0.0.1:<http>/block 200 http 127.0.0.1:<http>/block
http://n3.test:<http>/ failed
proxy: xn1.test:<http>
== an empty no_proxy reads NO_PROXY
http://h.test:<http>/ failed
